{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"e2f010886b6dab37b945bfe9a0cf192abf048ccba33a2290d1638dc364f0612c","slug":"introducing-the-technical-notes","location":"/articles/introducing-the-technical-notes/introducing-the-technical-notes.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Introducing Underworld Technical Notes","description":"The writing on this site that people want to cite now has its own series. A technical note is written like a short paper, gets an archival PDF, and carries a DOI that resolves to it.","banner":"/underworldcode.org-preview/c468a06e88/build/banner-6715d4f13aa83d11bc6278f2f49e7505.jpg","keywords":["Underworld Code"],"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Louis Moresi","given":"Louis","family":"Moresi"},"name":"Louis Moresi","orcid":"0000-0003-3685-174X","affiliations":["Australian National University"],"id":"contributors-introducing-the-technical-notes-generated-uid-0"}],"affiliations":[{"id":"Australian National University","name":"Australian National University"}],"date":"2026-08-14","license":{"content":{"id":"CC-BY-4.0","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","name":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","free":true,"CC":true}},"open_access":true,"github":"https://github.com/underworld-technical-notes/underworldcode.org","numbering":{"title":{"offset":2}},"source_url":"https://github.com/underworld-technical-notes/underworldcode.org/blob/main/articles/introducing-the-technical-notes/introducing-the-technical-notes.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/underworld-technical-notes/underworldcode.org/edit/main/articles/introducing-the-technical-notes/introducing-the-technical-notes.md","thumbnail":"/underworldcode.org-preview/c468a06e88/build/banner-6715d4f13aa83d11bc6278f2f49e7505.jpg","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"introducing-the-technical-notes.md","url":"/underworldcode.org-preview/c468a06e88/build/introducing-the-tech-8769726a231ce48b2b47cb4797e5b54e.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"div","class":"uwtn-banner","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/underworldcode.org-preview/c468a06e88/build/banner-6715d4f13aa83d11bc6278f2f49e7505.jpg","key":"vQ3gwVwVU7","urlSource":"figures/banner.jpg"},{"type":"div","class":"uwtn-credit","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Photo by ","key":"y2OE2GA1Op"},{"type":"link","url":"https://unsplash.com/@lukashron?utm_source=underworld-technical-notes&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=api-credit","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lukas Hron","key":"RJV8iG1WAq"}],"urlSource":"https://unsplash.com/@lukashron?utm_source=underworld-technical-notes&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=api-credit","key":"V4tX6w5bBn"},{"type":"text","value":" / ","key":"xm9DyMkaVG"},{"type":"link","url":"https://unsplash.com/?utm_source=underworld-technical-notes&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=api-credit","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unsplash","key":"xZre3wQcwY"}],"urlSource":"https://unsplash.com/?utm_source=underworld-technical-notes&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=api-credit","key":"GkgQ8z6ud2"}],"key":"jZO1M9WPep"}],"key":"zAo47TTyEY"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Our underworld web site has always carried two kinds of writing. Some of it is news — a\nrelease, a workshop, a paper accepted. The rest is the sort of thing a reader\nlater wants to point at: how a solver behaves, what a benchmark\nmeasured and what it demonstrates, why a method works the way it does and\nwhere it stops working. The two have been mixed together, and there has been\nno way to cite the second kind.","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"J6yhTkak9I"}],"key":"zirsABjnlM"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"So we now have ","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"sanAOEk10U"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"technical notes","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"NIsnnTMZ3s"}],"key":"xMaMoBEdSQ"},{"type":"text","value":" that are written like a short\npaper or perhaps a preprint. Each one carries a version, an archival PDF built from the same source as the\npage, and a DOI that resolves to that PDF. Deposit is deliberate rather than\nautomatic: a note is published here first, and only gets an identifier when we\ndecide it is worth one.","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"CNaRVuPJjj"}],"key":"LhwleKTlnO"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The point is for us to write down what we have created with enough content\nto be useful and not a lot more, and then refer to it — from a paper, from an\nissue, from the next note; instead of describing it again. Not quite\ndocumentation and not yet a research publication.","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"fAnjxKDx1T"}],"key":"C7iyOv3ffZ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first two are up: ","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"c8yi5gSxHv"},{"type":"link","url":"/moving-the-mesh-without-remaking-it/","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Moving the Mesh Without\nRemaking It","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"PynJz9EHRF"}],"urlSource":"/moving-the-mesh-without-remaking-it/","key":"qRKEHdfLTk"},{"type":"text","value":", on redistributing mesh\nnodes to follow the physics without remeshing, and ","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"c9Rxpa9M9T"},{"type":"link","url":"/running-underworld-in-a-browser/","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Running Underworld in a\nBrowser","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"lsn24m80Me"}],"urlSource":"/running-underworld-in-a-browser/","key":"eeEkQE2fTU"},{"type":"text","value":", on launching any repository at any\nversion without installing anything.","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"ahGpGFwAFb"}],"key":"zSfu2myUXC"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Everything written before is still here, at the same addresses. The fifty posts\nthat already carry DOIs keep them, and those DOIs still resolve.","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"JkSgIGl9wj"}],"key":"go6bFmEUYJ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":49,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you work with Underworld and have something worth writing down, the notes\nare open to you — ","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"key":"fKc8Ia2QCj"},{"type":"link","url":"/submit/","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"how to submit one","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"key":"LM4mvzhv9g"}],"urlSource":"/submit/","key":"NdRXwy3dpV"},{"type":"text","value":". You can read ","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"key":"bZ2trQIHz4"},{"type":"link","url":"/notes","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"all of\nthem","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"key":"bcNkE3Amj5"}],"urlSource":"/notes/","dataUrl":"/notes.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"c83lNgMIqM"},{"type":"text","value":", or ","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"key":"vYqxIrWQR4"},{"type":"link","url":"/topics/","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"browse by topic","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"key":"HJZWMYFnRC"}],"urlSource":"/topics/","key":"SjwXdl7UXI"},{"type":"text","value":".","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"key":"okHUEJY62s"}],"key":"dbpjlX9Y3v"},{"type":"div","class":"uwtn-discuss","children":[{"type":"div","class":"uwtn-discuss-head","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comments","key":"UdZtps4oAl"}],"key":"CVqPDT4gJn"},{"type":"div","class":"uwtn-discuss-body","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Discussion of these notes happens in GitHub Discussions, so it stays with the source and is searchable alongside it.","key":"IW4UyKG2aT"}],"key":"mkXWEYDNBW"},{"type":"div","class":"uwtn-discuss-links","children":[{"type":"link","url":"https://github.com/Underworld-Technical-Notes/underworldcode.org/discussions?discussions_q=introducing-the-technical-notes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read the discussion","key":"KMJEvGztnR"}],"urlSource":"https://github.com/Underworld-Technical-Notes/underworldcode.org/discussions?discussions_q=introducing-the-technical-notes","error":true,"key":"QWY3HwDFNV"},{"type":"link","url":"https://github.com/Underworld-Technical-Notes/underworldcode.org/discussions/new?category=general&title=introducing-the-technical-notes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start one","key":"nZWIaLCjqv"}],"urlSource":"https://github.com/Underworld-Technical-Notes/underworldcode.org/discussions/new?category=general&title=introducing-the-technical-notes","error":true,"key":"kFInzfaLLP"}],"key":"AvKs3LQwOy"}],"key":"tIBjgHwOEV"}],"k